  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hydration power energy <math><mo>&#8733;</mo></math>&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>q</mtext> <mtext>1</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>q</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mrow><mo>(</mo> <mrow> <mfrac> <mtext>1</mtext> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>r</mtext> <mo>+</mo> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mtext>+</mtext><mfrac> <mtext>1</mtext> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>r</mtext> <mo>&#8722;</mo> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> <mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow> </math><br /><br /><math><mo>&#8756;</mo></math> Solubility order of IIA group element sulphates in water:<br /><br /><math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">S</mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>4</mn></mrow></msub></math><br /><br />Generally bigger size ion form&nbsp;a strong bond with bigger ion so solubility will decrease or smaller the cation, greater the hydration sphere.&nbsp;<br />Hence, Solubility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></math> ion with alkali or alkaline earth metal decrease top to bottom.",
